{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 55, :comments ["<b>For barbs in your eyes</b> — pegs that bore out your eyes. The Aramaic translation of pegs is שִׂכִּים. And as for וְלִצְנִינִים, the commentators explain it in the sense of a thorn-hedge surrounding you, to confine and imprison you so that there is no going out or coming in — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Numbers 33:55). Now it is clear that שִׂכִּים means sharp thorns, from the language of \"remove its thorn-hedge\" (Isaiah 5:5), \"I will hedge up your way\" (Hosea 2:8), \"Did You not make a hedge about him\" (Job 1:10), \"and put a knife to your throat\" (Proverbs 23:2) — something sharp, of thorn or of iron. וְלִצְנִינִים is likewise an inflaming thorn-bush, from the language of \"and the thirsty take them among thorns\" (Job 5:5), \"Thorns, snares are in the way of the perverse\" (Proverbs 22:5) — which lack the doubled letter. But the intent of שִׂכִּים בְּעֵינֵיכֶם is to lead you astray so that you do not see and do not understand, as in \"for a bribe blinds the clear-sighted\" (Exodus 23:8), and likewise \"you shall not put a stumbling block before the blind\" (Leviticus 19:14), according to the opinion of our Rabbis (Torat Kohanim, Kedoshim, parashah 2:14). He says that they will bore out your eyes to lead you astray so that you do not see and do not understand, and they will train you in all their abominations and to serve their elohim, as He said: \"They shall not dwell in your land, lest they cause you to sin against Me, for you will serve their elohim\" (Exodus 23:33). And after they have become barbs in your eyes and have led you astray to turn away from following Me, they will be thorns in your sides that will cause you pain and distress you, to plunder and despoil you. And afterward, \"and they shall harass you\" — they will wage war against you and besiege you, and I will exile you from before them into a complete exile. For just as I intended to do to them through you — that they would all be driven from the land and you would leave none of them there — but you did not hearken to My voice, so will I do to you, and I will not leave even one of you in the land. And in this same sense Joshua said (Joshua 23:13): \"And they shall be snares and traps to you, and scourges in your sides, and thorns in your eyes, until you perish from off this good land.\" He said \"snares and traps\" concerning the error into which they will lead you astray, as in \"for you will serve their elohim, and it will become a snare to you\"; \"and scourges in your sides\" — that they will chastise you with whips to plunder and despoil and cause great pain; \"and thorns in your eyes\" — that is the blinding of the eyes of the heart to stray yet further after their elohim, until they perish from upon the earth, as in the matter of \"lest they see with their eyes and hear with their ears and understand with their heart and return and be healed\" (Isaiah 6:10)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:10:26.623692215Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}